#!/usr/bin/env sh
# A merge may not silently delete the other side's committed work.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This hook closes a gap that several documents and no code had closed. The rule —
# "a merge must not hand `main` back its own older content" — was written down in
# `docs/ORCHESTRATION.md`, copied verbatim into two `.skills/` files, pointed at from
# three more, and asserted nowhere. The one automated check it had was a `comm -13`
# recipe an agent was expected to remember, in a document AGENTS.md does not mention,
# which reports hundreds of innocent paths when run at the only moment it could act
# and misses the shape that actually cost this repository 17 files and 1,835 lines.
#
# It lives here because this is the last moment the damage is still free to undo, and
# because it is the one moment git guarantees to run code in for a merge. `pre-commit`
# cannot see it: `tsc` and `build` both pass a reverted file, since a reverted file is
# a perfectly good file. That is the whole reason `gate:verify` did not catch it.
#
# WHY IT IS A GATE AND NOT A REPORT. `.husky/post-merge` deliberately cannot fail —
# by the time it runs the merge is recorded. This one runs BEFORE the merge commit is
# written, so a non-zero exit leaves nothing landed and nothing to undo. A merge that
# reports success while deleting another branch's work is worse than one that stops.
#
# WHAT IT CANNOT COVER, stated here so nobody relies on it:
# - A FAST-FORWARD landing fires no hook at all. That path is safe by construction —
#   the branch tip contains main as an ancestor, so the result IS the branch tree and
#   every difference from main is a change the branch made on purpose. Verified with
#   raw git, not assumed.
# - `--no-verify` bypasses this, as it bypasses every other gate in this repository.
#   CI is the backstop for that, and this is the floor under it rather than the ceiling.
# - The incoming ref is read from GIT_REFLOG_ACTION because MERGE_HEAD is not yet
#   written in this hook. If it cannot be identified the guard REFUSES rather than
#   passing: a check that cannot tell must not report success.
#
# `HUSKY=0` is handled by the dispatcher in scripts/install-git-hooks.js.
node scripts/merge-takeover-guard.mjs